Chapter: GconCompileReadPathTest
  cites Works chapter GopConsole
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A8. `gcon-compile` used to test VT-x above the ESP mount and both file reads,
 and codex-vm's guest sees no VT-x, so the bed took that refusal every time and
 the mount, the reads, the conversion and the byte-count report below it could
 not be reached from anywhere. Main 18368 moved the check to just above
 `vm-compile-cdx`, the only caller that needs it. The two arms were hand-run
 under `build\desk.ps1` and written into `DeskBuildLoop.md` as prose, which is
 a claim with no runner.

 THIS TEST TAKES NO `.disk` SIDECAR AND MUST NOT BE GIVEN ONE. `no FAT volume
 on the boot medium` is the PASS, not a missing fixture (L-SIDECAR runs the
 other way here). It is the whole discrimination: reaching the mount at all is
 what proves the VT-x check is no longer above it. With the check restored to
 its old position the same run answers `VT-x is locked off in firmware`
 instead, and the mount never happens -- measured both ways 2026-08-21.

 Attaching a real ESP would report the two byte counts, which is a richer
 reading and a worse test: the counts move with every seed refresh, so the
 sidecar would have to be re-minted for changes that have nothing to do with
 this path. `DeskBuildLoop.md` records that measurement and the command.

  gcr-rows : Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Console] Integer
  gcr-rows (ns) (i) (n) =
    if i >= n then 0
    else act
      print-line-uni ("  | " & gcon-row-text ns i)
      gcr-rows ns (i + 1) n
    end

  opening : [Console, Device.Port] Nothing =
    let ns = alloc-zeroed 64 64
    in let i0 = gcon-init ns
    in act
      c0 <- gcon-compile ns ""
      print-line-uni ("no argument, lines : " & integer-to-text (gcon-count ns))
      r0 <- gcr-rows ns 0 (gcon-count ns)
      c1 <- gcon-compile ns "SRC/INDEX.TXT"
      print-line-uni ("with a path, lines : " & integer-to-text (gcon-count ns))
      r1 <- gcr-rows ns 0 (gcon-count ns)
      print-line-uni "done"
    end
